    "result_text": "All 14 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no registration date is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both settable on create and returned in responses; the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` map it to `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After mapping the incoming DTO, if `registrationDate` is null (none supplied) it's set to `LocalDate.now()`; a supplied value is preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is what backs persistence.\n\nMapStruct auto-maps `registrationDate` by name in both directions, so no mapper change was needed. The V2 controller only serves `/v2/owners`, so it was unaffected.",
